      "summary": "add index on users.last_seen_at (migration 20261015)"
    }
  ],
  "ground_truth": {
    "root_cause": "A schema migration deployed with commit d4e5f6a created an index on users.last_seen_at as a blocking operation on an ~80M-row table. The CREATE INDEX held an AccessExclusiveLock on the users table for its duration, blocking all writes. Every operation that writes to users - signups, profile updates, the last_seen_at touch on login - stalled and hit the 5s statement timeout. Reads were unaffected. Recovery required cancelling the migration to release the lock.",
    "evidence_path": [
      "deploy d4e5f6a to users-service at 20:09 ships migration 20261015 (add index on users.last_seen_at)",
      "users-db INFO at 20:10: migration started, CREATE INDEX on an ~80M-row table",
      "users-db WARN: 40+ sessions blocked on AccessExclusiveLock for relation users",
      "users-service write queries time out (statement_timeout 5s); signups and profile updates fail",
      "recovery immediately after the migration is cancelled and locks release"
    ],
    "fix": "Cancel the blocking migration (done). Re-run it as an online, non-blocking index build (CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY). Add a pre-deploy check that flags blocking DDL against large tables and requires an online alternative or a maintenance window.",
    "should_escalate": false
  }
}
